  "methodology": "Online backup of validated SCIP facts. Setup deterministically reshards existing immutable claims into <=2000-claim owners with identical context/fingerprint and copied physical inputs/selectors; no fact/support/provenance is altered. This is a storage workload, not a claim that the original provider can reindex those shards. Original ownership and reshaped ownership both receive a complete first publication from empty projections with the current physical schema. Complete first publication and 3 serial replacements each of 1/10/100 full shards use the production publisher, WAL/FULL, all indexes, support checks and commit. Replacements validate every fact through addFact under a changed synthetic input fingerprint; staging/seal time is reported separately. No pointer-only timing, cache eviction or compiler/LOC claim. Full ownership EXCEPT oracles and pinned history are checked outside timing. High-fanout supports use synthetic derived dependency facts and alternate proofs. Source bytes remain unchanged.",
